/E (The 2026 challenge, REBUILT presented by Haas, asks teams to design and build a robot that maximizes points through different strategic actions.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
552 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 437 0 R
/E (We identified two main ways to score: shooting balls \(fuel\) into the alliance hub, and climbing the tower at the end of the match. Each action has a different value, so from day one we analyzed which offered the most scoring potential relative to the time available in a match.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
553 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 437 0 R
/E (The match has an autonomous period and a teleoperated period, so the robot must perform actions both automatically and under driver control. We focused our analysis on how to use each stage of the match to maximize the efficiency of the system.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
554 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 437 0 R
/E (Instead of designing a robot that could do every possible action, we chose to prioritize the actions that generate points consistently throughout the match. That became the foundation of our strategy.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
