570 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 438 0 R
/E (Points come mainly from shooting fuel into the hub, where every shot that goes in adds to the alliance score. We identified shooting speed and consistency as the key factors for maximizing points in a match.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
571 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 438 0 R
/E (We also analyzed the end-of-match climb, which awards additional points. However, it requires dedicated time and an additional mechanism. Based on this analysis, we decided to focus our design on optimizing the shooter, prioritizing the ability to score continuously instead of depending on a single end-game action.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
572 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 439 0 R
/E (Match structure)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
573 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 439 0 R
/E (A match is divided into stages in which the robot must perform different actions. First comes the autonomous period, where the robot runs only on its programming. Then the teleoperated period begins, where drivers control the robot to move around the field, collect balls and shoot at the target. The robot's performance also depends on coordination with its alliance partners, so from the start we considered how important it is to contribute steadily to the alliance's total score. Based on this, we focused the robot's design on actions it could perform continuously during both phases of the match.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
