576 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 439 0 R
/E (One of the main challenges was building a system that could shoot balls quickly and consistently. Our analysis showed that poor fuel alignment inside the robot could cause jams or inaccurate shots, significantly reducing the system's efficiency. Another major challenge was mobility: the robot had to move quickly and cross obstacles like the bump without losing stability. From these challenges, the team defined three main design criteria:)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
577 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 439 0 R
/E (Speed, to collect and shoot balls in the shortest possible time. Storage capacity, to keep a continuous flow of fuel. Shooting consistency, to reduce errors and maximize points.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
578 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 439 0 R
/E (These criteria guided the team's engineering decisions and became the foundation of the robot's strategy.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
