830 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 463 0 R
/E (We divided the robot into independent subsystems to optimize the design, simplify iteration and make sure each component had a specific role in the fuel flow. This let us design, build and improve each mechanism more clearly, understanding how it interacts with the others.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
831 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 463 0 R
/E (The main subsystems are the drivebase, which moves the robot; the intake, which picks balls up from the floor; the feeder, which carries fuel inside the robot; the shooter, which launches the balls at the target; and the extendable hopper, which stores more balls during the match.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
832 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 463 0 R
/E (Each subsystem was designed around the team's strategy, the speed the game demands and the need to handle many balls without jamming. During development, these systems were tested and tuned repeatedly to improve performance and make sure they worked as one integrated robot.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
833 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 463 0 R
/E (The main goal was a robot that could collect, store and shoot fuel quickly and consistently, a key part of our strategy for REBUILT.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [5]
>>
